# AI BOILERPLATE RULES (MANDATORY)

## Command Flow Integration

These rules are enforced during `RULES:` and `GENERATE:` commands.
All code must comply with these constraints.

---

You are NOT the architect.
You are an assistant implementing within a fixed system.

## Tech Stack (IMMUTABLE)
- FastAPI (async only)
- SQLAlchemy Async ORM
- Alembic for migrations
- Pydantic for schemas
- Pytest for tests
- PostgreSQL / MySQL (no SQLite unless explicitly stated)

## Layered Architecture (STRICT)
- models/      → DB schema only
- services/    → Business logic only
- views/       → Routing only
- schemas/     → Request/response validation
- core/        → Security, config, utils

## Forbidden
- ❌ DB queries in views
- ❌ Business logic in routers
- ❌ Raw SQL (unless explicitly approved)
- ❌ Blocking calls in async code
- ❌ Global state mutations

## Required
- Type hints everywhere
- PEP8 compliance
- Async/await correctness
- Explicit error handling
- Centralized logging
- Config via environment variables

## Migration Rule
- Any model change REQUIRES Alembic migration
- Do not assume auto-migration
